{"content":[{"c":["ACHOR"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Valley that received its name when Achan, the troubler of Israel, was stoned and burned there (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.7.24-26","r":"Josh.7.24-26","rawR":"Josh.7.24-26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.7.24-26","value":"Josh.7.24-26"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 7:24-26"},"; cf. ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.2.7","r":"1Chr.2.7","rawR":"1Chr.2.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.2.7","value":"1Chr.2.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 2:7"},"). Achor was on the northern boundary of Judah’s tribal allotment (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.15.7","r":"Josh.15.7","rawR":"Josh.15.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.15.7","value":"Josh.15.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 15:7"},"). Later, the valley is mentioned in prophecies of Israel’s future blessings. A valley once known as the scene of Israel’s trouble would become “a door of hope” and a place for joyful singing (",{"href":"?bref=Hos.2.15","r":"Hos.2.15","rawR":"Hos.2.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Hos.2.15","value":"Hos.2.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Hos 2:15"},"); a place of relative desolation would one day become a place for herds to lie down (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.65.10","r":"Isa.65.10","rawR":"Isa.65.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.65.10","value":"Isa.65.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 65:10"},"). The valley of Achor is commonly identified as the Buqei‘ah."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Achor","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jos 7:24-26","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.7.24-26","rawQueryValue":"Josh.7.24-26","sourceRefExact":"Josh.7.24-26"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 2:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.2.7","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.2.7","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.2.7"},{"anchorText":"Jos 15:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.15.7","rawQueryValue":"Josh.15.7","sourceRefExact":"Josh.15.7"},{"anchorText":"Hos 2:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Hos.2.15","rawQueryValue":"Hos.2.15","sourceRefExact":"Hos.2.15"},{"anchorText":"Is 65:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.65.10","rawQueryValue":"Isa.65.10","sourceRefExact":"Isa.65.10"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"b9dc3410504b639678f66a52103cfe9113c7d7533ebc0547da1e786ca5ee4143","sourceItemName":"Achor","sourceItemOrder":83,"sourceMember":"Articles/A.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Achor","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Achor","title":"Achor","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}